**Definition 27.1 (public center groups).** For each $n\ge1$ put

$$
m=m(n),\qquad r=n-m,\qquad
 a=\min\{\lfloor m/2\rfloor,r\},\qquad b=r-a.
\tag{GDB.108}
$$

The $m$ center positions are $a+1,\ldots,a+m$. Define a public name
map $g_n$ on the descriptors by

$$
g_n(j,e)=
\begin{cases}
2j-1+e,&1\le j\le a,\\
j-a,&a<j\le a+m,\\
2(j-a-m)-1+e,&a+m<j\le n,
\end{cases}
\qquad g_n(B)=2b+1.
\tag{GDB.109}
$$

Each name is an integer in $[m]=\{1,\ldots,m\}$. The two descriptors
at center $a+i$ have name $i$. Among the earlier positions there is
at most one descriptor of each name, and the same holds among the
later positions together with $B$.

